1
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:14,125
(Ryu Se-il)

2
00:00:20,333 --> 00:00:22,042
(Ha Jung-hoon)

3
00:00:27,792 --> 00:00:29,417
(Lee Jung-chan)

4
00:00:34,875 --> 00:00:36,625
(Jung Si-wan)

5
00:00:44,917 --> 00:00:46,708
"Boy, with Caution"

6
00:00:56,583 --> 00:00:57,917
So you're a guy.

7
00:00:58,542 --> 00:00:59,542
Yeah.

8
00:01:00,708 --> 00:01:02,958
I told you before that I was a guy.

9
00:01:04,542 --> 00:01:07,167
Did you? My memory isn't that great.

10
00:01:09,208 --> 00:01:10,917
Are you gonna run just because I'm a guy?

11
00:01:11,042 --> 00:01:12,042
Why would I run?

12
00:01:13,958 --> 00:01:15,792
It's actually more
interesting that you are.

13
00:01:17,375 --> 00:01:18,667
What's your name?

14
00:01:20,417 --> 00:01:21,917
I'm Kim Ji Tae.

15
00:01:28,625 --> 00:01:31,583
Do I have to explain the meaning of my name
before you tell me yours?

16
00:01:36,667 --> 00:01:37,917
I'm Jang Gi-woo.

17
00:01:41,875 --> 00:01:44,000
Does this guy have no friends?

18
00:01:44,125 --> 00:01:47,750
Mom, secretary, Mr. Jang Gi-woo.

19
00:01:53,458 --> 00:01:54,750
Jang Gi-woo?

20
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:07,083
What?

21
00:02:08,250 --> 00:02:10,458
Where are you right now?

22
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:15,042
I'm busy right now.

23
00:02:15,958 --> 00:02:17,500
I asked where you are.

24
00:02:17,625 --> 00:02:19,542
I told you, I'm busy.

25
00:02:20,708 --> 00:02:22,208
Gotta go.

26
00:02:25,375 --> 00:02:27,167
I'm glad I asked you out.

27
00:02:28,875 --> 00:02:31,292
Though you're not quite what I expected.

28
00:02:32,458 --> 00:02:35,000
So this is the kind of guy you are.

29
00:02:35,125 --> 00:02:36,333
Quite a surprise.

30
00:02:38,292 --> 00:02:39,792
What do you mean?

31
00:02:39,917 --> 00:02:41,542
I mean you're intriguing.

32
00:02:41,667 --> 00:02:42,875
Unique.

33
00:02:44,250 --> 00:02:46,500
I want to keep seeing you.

34
00:02:48,708 --> 00:02:50,875
What should I call you?

35
00:02:51,958 --> 00:02:53,250
How about "hyung"?

36
00:02:55,458 --> 00:02:56,792
Gi-woo hyung.

37
00:02:57,708 --> 00:02:59,083
Can I call you that?

38
00:03:05,167 --> 00:03:11,083
"Boy, with Caution"
(Episode 6)

39
00:03:21,083 --> 00:03:22,542
Hyeon-jae, long time no see.

40
00:03:24,583 --> 00:03:25,583
Beom.

41
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:30,292
Head over to Nagwon-dong.

42
00:03:41,042 --> 00:03:43,333
You really beat their faces to a pulp.

43
00:03:48,708 --> 00:03:50,167
Is Jang Gi-woo really all that?

44
00:03:52,750 --> 00:03:54,083
What did you say to him?

45
00:03:54,208 --> 00:03:56,083
You heard everything. Why ask?

46
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:59,458
I would've gotten you
a coffee if I'd known.

47
00:03:59,583 --> 00:04:00,958
Gi-woo hyung bought it.

48
00:04:12,792 --> 00:04:14,792
So that's your type.

49
00:04:15,917 --> 00:04:20,500
He's more uptight and dull than I thought.

50
00:04:29,625 --> 00:04:30,500
Where's my phone?

51
00:04:30,625 --> 00:04:31,750
I gave it to Jang Gi-woo.

52
00:04:38,667 --> 00:04:41,125
Just kidding. Did I scare you?

53
00:04:42,708 --> 00:04:43,851
Did you think I'd just hand it right back?

54
00:04:43,875 --> 00:04:45,708
I sank ten million into this.

55
00:04:46,208 --> 00:04:48,917
Plus the medical bills for
beating the hell out of those guys.

56
00:04:49,042 --> 00:04:52,167
And getting expelled
for taking the fall alone.

57
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:54,208
Not to mention emotional damages.

58
00:04:54,958 --> 00:04:59,208
Factor in the time and coffee money
for meeting Mr. Jang Gi-woo...

59
00:05:00,458 --> 00:05:01,917
Twenty million, and we call it even.

60
00:05:04,875 --> 00:05:06,250
And if I refuse to pay?

61
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:12,625
Figured you'd say that,
so I thought it through.

62
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:16,167
Can't just let a debtor walk away.
You need collateral.

63
00:05:16,458 --> 00:05:18,500
I don't have anything to give you.

64
00:05:22,125 --> 00:05:23,542
How could you not?

65
00:05:24,375 --> 00:05:25,875
Don't you still have Jang Gi-woo?

66
00:05:28,125 --> 00:05:30,625
Messing with your money,
your school, or your parents...

67
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:32,458
None of that bothers you, does it?

68
00:05:32,583 --> 00:05:35,417
I'll give you two days.

69
00:05:36,750 --> 00:05:39,125
If you don't cough up
the cash in two days...

70
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:40,875
your teacher is done for.

71
00:05:46,958 --> 00:05:48,333
How about that?

72
00:05:52,333 --> 00:05:53,875
Fine. Deal.

73
00:05:55,958 --> 00:05:58,333
Hey, I'm still curious about something.

74
00:05:58,958 --> 00:06:00,458
That chat...

75
00:06:01,042 --> 00:06:04,242
You knew it was Jang Gi-woo from the start
and started it on purpose, didn't you?

76
00:06:07,958 --> 00:06:09,292
Congratulations.

77
00:06:13,667 --> 00:06:15,875
You finally have something
you're afraid to lose.

78
00:06:36,042 --> 00:06:38,322
Why did you come all the
way here this late in the night?

79
00:06:45,292 --> 00:06:46,667
Did something happen?

80
00:06:46,792 --> 00:06:48,458
That chat...

81
00:06:48,583 --> 00:06:51,783
You knew it was Jang Gi-woo from the start
and started it on purpose, didn't you?

82
00:07:05,333 --> 00:07:11,000
I did it because I liked you.

83
00:07:15,458 --> 00:07:17,583
Please don't be mad.

84
00:07:28,125 --> 00:07:29,417
What do I have to do...

85
00:07:31,542 --> 00:07:32,958
to make you stop?

86
00:07:35,875 --> 00:07:36,875
All of this...

87
00:07:40,958 --> 00:07:42,542
I can't stop.

88
00:07:42,667 --> 00:07:43,917
Lee Hyeon-jae.

89
00:07:44,833 --> 00:07:48,000
Whether it's care or love,
I'll keep giving it to you.

90
00:07:50,833 --> 00:07:53,000
You don't have to do anything, sir.

91
00:07:54,792 --> 00:07:56,750
It's fine if you pretend not to notice.

92
00:08:07,125 --> 00:08:09,417
I've said all I wanted to say.

93
00:08:10,208 --> 00:08:11,708
I'll take off now.

94
00:08:49,042 --> 00:08:52,000
Hey, the other day...

95
00:08:54,125 --> 00:08:55,708
What did you give Kim Jeong-ha?

96
00:08:56,417 --> 00:08:57,042
What?

97
00:08:57,167 --> 00:08:59,375
Didn't you exchange something
with Kim Jeong-ha?

98
00:08:59,833 --> 00:09:01,125
I'm asking what it was.

99
00:09:01,542 --> 00:09:03,125
Nothing of that sort.

100
00:09:04,083 --> 00:09:05,250
We just talked for a bit.

101
00:09:05,375 --> 00:09:06,458
I heard you're doing drugs.

102
00:09:09,917 --> 00:09:11,333
Who told you that?

103
00:09:11,583 --> 00:09:14,333
I don't care if you're using or not.

104
00:09:14,792 --> 00:09:16,708
I hate Choi Young-moon anyway.

105
00:09:18,708 --> 00:09:20,042
And?

106
00:09:20,542 --> 00:09:22,750
- Then why are you asking?
- Because of Jeong-ha.

107
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:25,292
You know what Jeong-ha's into, right?

108
00:09:28,208 --> 00:09:29,368
You're not even close to him.

109
00:09:29,458 --> 00:09:30,958
We can start getting close now.

110
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,292
So spit it out.

111
00:09:38,542 --> 00:09:40,792
What the hell is he doing right now?

112
00:09:45,917 --> 00:09:48,437
If you keep slacking off like this,
who's gonna lend you money?

113
00:09:51,958 --> 00:09:53,500
I returned the suit and the bike keys.

114
00:09:53,625 --> 00:09:55,208
Pass a message to Kim Ji Tae for me.

115
00:09:55,625 --> 00:09:58,500
Once I give him Lee Hyeon-jae's phone,
our slate is wiped clean.

116
00:10:02,292 --> 00:10:03,434
Looks like we have a customer.

117
00:10:03,458 --> 00:10:04,917
I said the debt is settled.

118
00:10:05,625 --> 00:10:07,750
Kim Ji Tae never mentioned that to me.

119
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:29,792
It's true. You really are here.

120
00:10:31,792 --> 00:10:33,042
Get out.

121
00:10:34,250 --> 00:10:36,083
What if I came to borrow money?

122
00:10:36,458 --> 00:10:37,667
Got a minute?

123
00:10:39,417 --> 00:10:40,958
Let's go inside together.

124
00:10:41,250 --> 00:10:43,167
I told you, I'm here for a loan.

125
00:10:43,292 --> 00:10:45,434
Do you even know what kind of place this is
to come asking for money?

126
00:10:45,458 --> 00:10:47,578
Of course I know what this
place is, how could I not?

127
00:10:48,292 --> 00:10:49,667
Isn't it where you work?

128
00:10:51,250 --> 00:10:53,625
Hey! Are you buying or borrowing?

129
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:55,833
Tell him to get in here.

130
00:11:06,167 --> 00:11:07,458
Take this.

131
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:09,833
Didn't you say you'd do anything for money?

132
00:11:11,750 --> 00:11:14,417
Vending Machine, work for me instead.

133
00:11:17,083 --> 00:11:18,417
What?

134
00:11:20,583 --> 00:11:22,292
This is expensive.

135
00:11:22,417 --> 00:11:24,000
You can get good money if you sell it.

136
00:11:25,333 --> 00:11:27,208
Until that money runs out...

137
00:11:28,625 --> 00:11:30,375
stop doing this kind of work.

138
00:11:38,125 --> 00:11:39,542
Hey.

139
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:44,917
I'm not taking your damn
handouts, you fucker.

140
00:11:58,417 --> 00:11:59,667
Fuck!

141
00:12:01,250 --> 00:12:02,833
Then what do you want me to do?

142
00:12:16,958 --> 00:12:18,375
Sir.

143
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:20,143
Won't points get
deducted if we don't clean?

144
00:12:20,167 --> 00:12:21,458
Hyeon-jae ran off.

145
00:12:25,333 --> 00:12:27,059
I'll go bring him back.
You guys keep cleaning.

146
00:12:27,083 --> 00:12:28,208
Okay.

147
00:12:43,167 --> 00:12:45,750
I did it because I liked you.

148
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,167
Lee Hyeon-jae.

149
00:13:04,375 --> 00:13:06,625
I heard the guidance
counselor is taking over.

150
00:13:06,750 --> 00:13:08,167
It's Ms. Lee Ga-eun.

151
00:13:08,875 --> 00:13:09,875
That won't be necessary.

152
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,292
I already told Hyeon-jae
he doesn't need counseling.

153
00:13:13,708 --> 00:13:15,625
You're finally listening to reason.

154
00:13:15,750 --> 00:13:17,083
In just leaving Hyeon-jae alone.

155
00:13:19,125 --> 00:13:20,875
Even if it bothers you...

156
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,667
keeping your job comes first, right?

157
00:13:23,458 --> 00:13:27,333
Keep your head down and look the other way.

158
00:13:27,458 --> 00:13:29,208
Isn't that what you're best at?

159
00:13:51,292 --> 00:13:53,458
[Your mom looked for me at my work place.]

160
00:13:53,583 --> 00:13:55,023
Where is he? Tell him to hurry over!

161
00:13:55,083 --> 00:13:58,417
[She's also drunk.]
He's on his way. He should be here soon.

162
00:14:03,042 --> 00:14:05,167
Mom, let's talk after my shift.

163
00:14:05,292 --> 00:14:08,542
Neither of you care
how frantic I am, do you?

164
00:14:13,292 --> 00:14:14,167
Get up.

165
00:14:14,292 --> 00:14:15,542
Let go of me.

166
00:14:15,667 --> 00:14:18,708
I'm not leaving until you two reconsider.

167
00:14:19,208 --> 00:14:20,042
Just stand up first.

168
00:14:20,167 --> 00:14:22,083
Seriously...

169
00:14:22,750 --> 00:14:23,750
Mom.

170
00:14:23,833 --> 00:14:25,333
I said I'm not leaving.

171
00:14:30,125 --> 00:14:32,292
Let's talk at home.
Don't make a scene here.

172
00:14:32,417 --> 00:14:35,083
Don't bother trying to talk me out of it.

173
00:14:35,208 --> 00:14:37,042
I won't listen.

174
00:14:41,083 --> 00:14:42,458
Go back inside.

175
00:14:42,583 --> 00:14:44,458
I'll call the cops myself.

176
00:14:44,583 --> 00:14:47,125
The police? Why call the police?

177
00:14:47,250 --> 00:14:49,875
Why call the cops? That's humiliating.

178
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,934
- Isn't making a drunken scene humiliating enough?
- No, don't.

179
00:14:51,958 --> 00:14:53,750
Why on earth call the cops?

180
00:14:53,875 --> 00:14:56,042
Seriously, why call the cops?

181
00:14:56,167 --> 00:14:58,750
Then what do you want me to do?

182
00:15:09,417 --> 00:15:11,500
Mom, you're drunk right now.

183
00:15:11,917 --> 00:15:15,667
Let's go home.
I can't even face Ji-young right now.

184
00:15:21,583 --> 00:15:22,792
I'm begging you.

185
00:15:32,083 --> 00:15:37,083
If you just kept up appearances,
couldn't we go on living our lives?

186
00:15:38,583 --> 00:15:41,042
Why must you pull this
stunt every single time...

187
00:15:41,167 --> 00:15:43,958
when you'll just compromise
in the end anyway?

188
00:16:02,667 --> 00:16:04,417
You should've kept playing along.

189
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,708
Just like how you always
pretended not to notice.

190
00:16:13,375 --> 00:16:15,958
You knew full well what our problems were.

191
00:16:17,792 --> 00:16:19,434
You just didn't want people
talking behind our backs.

192
00:16:19,458 --> 00:16:22,167
That's why you looked the other way, right?

193
00:16:24,708 --> 00:16:26,125
If I keep playing dumb...

194
00:16:26,250 --> 00:16:30,292
can the two of you go
back to the way things were?

195
00:16:31,042 --> 00:16:32,333
The way things were?

196
00:16:32,458 --> 00:16:33,684
You mean the way you wanted them to be?

197
00:16:33,708 --> 00:16:37,292
Yes, the way I wanted! So what?

198
00:16:43,167 --> 00:16:47,000
You can't end up like me.

199
00:16:48,083 --> 00:16:53,000
I couldn't let people look down on you.

200
00:16:53,125 --> 00:16:55,000
Nobody in this world is perfect.

201
00:16:55,125 --> 00:16:56,833
Yes, there is. You are.

202
00:16:56,958 --> 00:16:58,917
That's how I raised you.

203
00:17:00,083 --> 00:17:01,542
Then you failed.

204
00:17:05,042 --> 00:17:07,002
I was so terrified of
scrutiny that I kept quiet.

205
00:17:07,042 --> 00:17:09,125
No matter what happened,
I just kept my mouth shut.

206
00:17:11,417 --> 00:17:14,208
I turned into a pathetic coward.

207
00:17:15,208 --> 00:17:17,542
Even knowing you were an alcoholic...

208
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:21,333
I couldn't even bring
myself to tell you to get help.

209
00:17:21,458 --> 00:17:22,750
Lower your voice.

210
00:17:24,917 --> 00:17:26,375
Mom, you know what?

211
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,917
In my life...

212
00:17:33,833 --> 00:17:36,208
the biggest flaw...

213
00:17:39,250 --> 00:17:40,708
is you.

214
00:17:51,917 --> 00:17:54,333
I'll settle the bill. Go straight home.

215
00:17:54,792 --> 00:17:56,333
You...

216
00:17:57,375 --> 00:17:58,750
You've changed.

217
00:17:59,792 --> 00:18:01,750
You weren't like this before.

218
00:18:03,333 --> 00:18:04,792
I've always been like this.

219
00:18:06,375 --> 00:18:08,208
You just never saw it.

220
00:18:09,458 --> 00:18:11,167
Hey...

221
00:18:24,933 --> 00:18:26,170
It was my first time...

222
00:18:29,830 --> 00:18:32,830
admitting my own flaws.

223
00:18:45,708 --> 00:18:47,250
And then...

224
00:18:49,567 --> 00:18:53,075
I thought of the person
who said he chose to live imperfectly.

225
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:16,833
Looking for something?

226
00:19:20,667 --> 00:19:22,083
Need money?

227
00:19:22,667 --> 00:19:24,458
- Yeah.
- How much?

228
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:26,375
Twenty million.

229
00:19:29,750 --> 00:19:31,875
I'll handle it. Come out first.

230
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,667
If you're gonna tell my dad,
I'll just sell this myself.

231
00:19:34,792 --> 00:19:36,500
I won't tell him.

232
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,375
Just step out first.

233
00:19:50,417 --> 00:19:52,000
Take care of it now.

234
00:19:53,792 --> 00:19:55,083
Right now.

235
00:19:58,208 --> 00:19:59,542
(Loan Consultation)

236
00:20:06,375 --> 00:20:08,833
That really was my last smoke, Hyeon-jong.

237
00:20:08,958 --> 00:20:10,667
Did I ask you to do something hard?

238
00:20:12,042 --> 00:20:13,917
I just told you to stick your tongue out.

239
00:20:14,042 --> 00:20:15,417
I'm sorry.

240
00:20:16,042 --> 00:20:18,417
Really, I'll pay you back tomorrow.

241
00:20:18,542 --> 00:20:20,625
Just one day. I swear,
just give me one day.

242
00:20:21,167 --> 00:20:23,458
Didn't I say I don't have an ashtray?

243
00:20:24,958 --> 00:20:26,458
Lend me yours too.

244
00:20:28,250 --> 00:20:29,500
Hyung.

245
00:20:30,250 --> 00:20:31,250
I'm busy right now.

246
00:20:31,333 --> 00:20:33,792
I know. Twenty million just cleared.

247
00:20:33,917 --> 00:20:35,250
Lee Hyeon-jae wired it.

248
00:20:38,750 --> 00:20:40,150
(Transfer: 20,000,000 KRW received)

249
00:20:46,792 --> 00:20:48,583
I'm in a good mood
today, so you get a pass.

250
00:20:48,708 --> 00:20:50,208
Pay me back tomorrow, Hyeon-jong.

251
00:20:55,542 --> 00:20:56,667
I'm heading out.

252
00:20:56,792 --> 00:20:57,917
Where to?

253
00:21:00,542 --> 00:21:02,125
Gotta drop off a phone.

254
00:21:04,125 --> 00:21:06,708
(Gi-woo hyung, want to meet
up? I have something for you.)

255
00:21:07,125 --> 00:21:09,708
Reply... Hurry up and reply.

256
00:21:11,958 --> 00:21:13,375
Want to come over to where I am?

257
00:21:14,458 --> 00:21:15,625
Okay.

258
00:21:29,083 --> 00:21:30,667
Your eyes are totally spaced out.

259
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,625
How'd you know I like that kind of look?

260
00:21:36,375 --> 00:21:37,958
A beer, please.

261
00:21:43,542 --> 00:21:46,000
My job is dealing with people like this.

262
00:21:49,292 --> 00:21:50,917
There's a job like that?

263
00:22:01,125 --> 00:22:02,750
Looks like tonight...

264
00:22:03,417 --> 00:22:05,250
you just wanted someone around.

265
00:22:05,375 --> 00:22:06,917
My timing's pretty good, isn't it?

266
00:22:09,583 --> 00:22:10,958
I guess so.

267
00:22:13,208 --> 00:22:15,500
Someone did cross my mind...

268
00:22:17,833 --> 00:22:20,167
but I couldn't call him over.

269
00:22:23,417 --> 00:22:24,917
Afraid I'd be found out.

270
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,500
So you've fallen for someone.

271
00:22:36,250 --> 00:22:37,833
I don't know.

272
00:22:37,958 --> 00:22:40,708
Poor Hyeon-jae.

273
00:22:42,292 --> 00:22:43,958
His heart's gonna break.

274
00:22:46,333 --> 00:22:48,708
His teacher has feelings for someone else.

275
00:22:58,125 --> 00:22:59,708
Give this to him for me.

276
00:23:03,750 --> 00:23:06,208
I wanted to play around
with you a bit longer, sir...

277
00:23:07,167 --> 00:23:08,625
but I got my money.

278
00:23:08,750 --> 00:23:10,375
So game over.

279
00:23:13,083 --> 00:23:14,833
That account named Sunflower...

280
00:23:16,917 --> 00:23:19,292
The person chatting with
you all this time wasn't me.

281
00:23:23,958 --> 00:23:25,292
It was...

282
00:23:26,792 --> 00:23:28,000
Lee Hyeon-jae.

283
00:23:29,125 --> 00:23:32,583
Lee Hyeon-jae from your school.

284
00:23:36,708 --> 00:23:38,167
Fascinating, isn't it?

285
00:23:51,208 --> 00:23:52,458
Cheers.

286
00:24:02,458 --> 00:24:04,750
He's always been kind of gloomy.

287
00:24:12,375 --> 00:24:14,208
Is it because he got beat up growing up?

288
00:24:14,875 --> 00:24:16,292
Did you send it?

289
00:24:19,417 --> 00:24:20,750
Is it over?

290
00:24:24,870 --> 00:24:27,716
They must've appproached you on
purpose right? From the very start...

291
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:35,500
Yeah, the money's been transferred.

292
00:24:39,458 --> 00:24:43,083
He said to get the phone from Jang Gi-woo.

293
00:24:48,405 --> 00:24:49,839
He'll probably go look for you tonight.

294
00:24:55,375 --> 00:24:56,917
Anyone here?

295
00:25:02,083 --> 00:25:03,417
Sir.

296
00:25:08,292 --> 00:25:09,542
Sir?

297
00:25:16,869 --> 00:25:17,869
Sir...

298
00:25:25,208 --> 00:25:27,125
Sir, have you been drinking?

299
00:26:01,208 --> 00:26:02,667
"Boy, with Caution"

300
00:26:03,167 --> 00:26:05,833
(Preview) Messing with someone
as dull and ordinary as me...

301
00:26:05,958 --> 00:26:07,333
Was that fun for you?

302
00:26:07,458 --> 00:26:08,667
Did it make you waver?

303
00:26:08,792 --> 00:26:10,333
You're not that important to me.

304
00:26:10,458 --> 00:26:12,458
Have you guys seen this on Instagram?

305
00:26:12,583 --> 00:26:14,458
Isn't Jang Gi-woo a repeat offender?

306
00:26:14,917 --> 00:26:17,375
I told you not to get
so emotionally invested.

307
00:26:17,500 --> 00:26:18,500
Say it yourself.

308
00:26:18,542 --> 00:26:19,809
Or do you want me to say it first?

309
00:26:19,833 --> 00:26:21,458
I can't treat you like I used to.

310
00:26:23,208 --> 00:26:24,000
Who is Lee Hyeon-jae?

311
00:26:24,125 --> 00:26:26,292
I heard he's the chairman's son.

312
00:26:26,417 --> 00:26:27,875
How am I supposed to believe this?

313
00:26:28,917 --> 00:26:30,167
I need to see it for myself.

314
00:26:31,125 --> 00:26:33,833
Loving someone can
turn out to be a mistake...

315
00:26:35,083 --> 00:26:36,250
Now I finally understand.
